<title>UK: MVI to end UK imports of Lada vehicles.</title>
<headline>MVI to end UK imports of Lada vehicles.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Inchcape Motors International said on Thursday that the Lada car import business of its unit Motor Vehicle Imports Ltd (MVI) will close, ending 24 years of imports of the Russian made car to the UK.</p>
<p>MVI had already announced that Lada producer AvtoVaz would not be able to restore its supply of suitable specified Lada vehicles to the UK.</p>
<p>Talks with a third party about taking over the car importer then fell through after a formal offer for MVI was withdrawn. The closure of the import business sees the loss of 70 jobs.</p>
<p>Inchcape Motors, which is owned by Inchcape Plc, said existing Lada owners will continue to receive full support on aftersales activities.</p>
<p>MVI has just 1,000 Lada vehicles left in company and dealer stock.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
